  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Phthalylsulfathiazole is a sulfonamide antibiotic used as an intestinal antiinfective, for example to treat diarrhoea or gut infections. It is an approved drug, though it is an older sulfonamide that is now little used and not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4493189&quot;>Wikidata Q4493189</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>phthalylsulfathiazole</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A07AB02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13248&quot;>DB13248</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4806&quot;>4806</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:9336&quot;>9336</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4493189&quot;>Q4493189</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C17H13N3O5S2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>403.427 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
